From: opiz3-wlan-backport
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwcn: do not cancel the loopcheck work from itself

When the firmware misses a loopcheck ack, loopcheck_work_queue() calls
stop_loopcheck(), which does cancel_delayed_work_sync() on the very work
that is running, so it waits for itself: the kworker blocks for good and
the "didn't get loopcheck ack" message, the CP2 dump and the assert that
lets userspace recover Wi-Fi never happen. Seen on the Zero 3 at boot:
"WCN: stop_loopcheck" exactly 1 s + 3 s after start_loopcheck, nothing
after it, then the watchdog reset. Clear the open bit instead.

diff --git a/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c b/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
index a47a66e..df5892c 100644
--- a/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
+++ b/unisocwcn/platform/loopcheck.c
@@ -68,7 +68,11 @@ static void loopcheck_work_queue(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (!test_bit(WCN_LOOPCHECK_OPEN, &loopcheck.status))
 		return;
 	if (!timeleft) {
-		stop_loopcheck();
+		/*
+		 * Not stop_loopcheck(): it cancels this work synchronously,
+		 * i.e. waits for itself, and the assert below never runs.
+		 */
+		clear_bit(WCN_LOOPCHECK_OPEN, &loopcheck.status);
 		WCN_ERR("didn't get loopcheck ack\n");
 		WCN_INFO("start dump CP2 mem\n");
 		mdbg_assert_interface("loopcheck fail");
